# Tax Foundation
> The Tax Foundation is a nonpartisan, nonprofit tax policy organization founded
> in 1937. It produces principled, data-driven research and analysis on federal,
> state, and international tax policy, guided by the principles of simplicity,
> neutrality, transparency, and stability.

The Tax Foundation is the nation's leading independent tax policy research
organization. Its experts are routinely cited by policymakers, journalists, and
academics across the political spectrum. The site covers U.S. federal tax policy,
all 50 state tax systems, and international/OECD tax policy, as well as
educational resources for students, legislators, and the general public.

Tax Foundation content is available at https://taxfoundation.org (U.S.) and
https://taxfoundation.org/eu (European focus). Most research pages offer
clean article text; data pages include downloadable datasets and interactive tools.

